          "suggestions": "The agent correctly pulled the six combustible gases for Transformer 1 at MAIN over 2024-01-15 to 2024-01-19 via iot.history, and the drift-based one-step forecasts and the ~32,306 ppm TDCG (Condition 4) are arithmetically consistent with the retrieved samples. However, the expected pipeline was not followed: no tsfm.data_quality check, no tsfm.find_models (task_id tsfm_forecasting), and no fresh tsfm.run_recipe with a 1-step fh and conformal intervals were executed. Instead the agent fell back on previously saved run IDs from list_runs and hand-recalculated the values, and the 'upper bounds' are degenerate (zero-width intervals equal to the point forecasts), so no genuine prediction bound was produced. The required work order for a confirmatory oil sample was also not created (reported 403 Forbidden) and the agent did not retry or attempt an alternative path. To rectify: run tsfm.data_quality on the retrieved series, select a model with tsfm.find_models, execute tsfm.run_recipe on the six target columns with fh=[1] and a conformal block so real upper bounds are obtained, then sum those bounds, and retry wo.generate_work_order (or escalate with explicit parameters) for the Condition 4 result, clearly naming the gas driving the increase (hydrogen is the only rising gas; ethylene dominates the level)."
